Subject: [PATCH] Admit stateless audio contexts at completed LLM cache boundaries

Gemma4 12B's adapter-less encoder is classified as streaming even though
its sole src_inputs input and features output retain no state between
whole-utterance Encode calls. The previous blanket AudioContext guard
therefore rejected completed direct-audio conversations.

Add a checkpoint-only capability that defaults to unsupported. The LiteRT
implementation admits only an unbuffered encoder with that actual layout,
no adapter or overlap, and empty live/stored audio contexts. Advanced
audio sessions remain unsupported because their EncodeAudio operations
do not establish the ordinary session's completed-turn boundary.

Try-acquire the audio lease before any context mutation and reuse it
through the existing context switch. No token-loop bookkeeping or audio
state copies are added. Tests cover real stateless-encoder continuation,
retained/stateful/buffered rejection, and nonblocking lease retry.

Base: google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM 5f25078c9439e176615af5ba42636ed904fca847
Apply after 0001-0011 in the LiteRT-LM patch sequence.

